{"appendix":false,"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:f30c07ca18e6d92538340ca4aaace062eeb8718202bfa9f1da0a2222f2f8d7f2","grain":"paper-statement","id":"Area-controlled-end-replacement-and-the-Bondi-Penrose-inequality-in-the-CKS-class-September-27-2026#prop:replacement","title":"Area-controlled end replacement"},"credit":{"kind":"producer-declared","license":null,"license_status":"consult-source-notice","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","source":"lean/formalization.yaml","source_registry":"index.json#/sources"},"detail":{"path":"../rows/cc41f7a2ce9ffcdc244392cc.json","pointer":"/row"},"display":"Theorem","generation_id":"sha256:fda4c3462963b650c538e2177794811eb1c221b267efea4b091fd6e397533f81","id":"r:Area-controlled-end-replacement-and-the-Bondi-Penrose-inequality-in-the-CKS-class-September-27-2026:prop:replacement","kind":"statement-detail","manuscript_id":"p:Area-controlled-end-replacement-and-the-Bondi-Penrose-inequality-in-the-CKS-class-September-27-2026","name":"Area-controlled end replacement","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","printed_number":"1.1","printed_number_provenance":{"atlas_pin":"c0851ae4ba3e12b1170cd4cdae33b48fae15d9a0","binding":{"file":"build/sections/00-introduction.tex","label":"prop:replacement","line":128,"manuscript":"Area-controlled-end-replacement-and-the-Bondi-Penrose-inequality-in-the-CKS-class-September-27-2026","statement_sha256":"079cb80f639fa1e00cd4c0abca0226f5471e1fb8f1b496bbbaabc18c74d25ce9"},"blob_sha256":"sha256:253ae0683558fd095a71d6f47ab0694d8d98b846c1a65d2bbf9b145d484af567","kind":"reading-page-computed","pdf_verified":false,"pin":"c0851ae4ba3e12b1170cd4cdae33b48fae15d9a0","renderer":"scripts/build_papers.py","source":"data/statement_numbers.json","upstream_pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb"},"printed_number_status":"recorded","reading_page":"papers/Area-controlled-end-replacement-and-the-Bondi-Penrose-inequality-in-the-CKS-class-September-27-2026.html#prop:replacement","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Replacing the end and retaining the area","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:1dd389f96e686b661882cb33fca7c288edc0c3ccfcd57ea7f23e2d0b70d010fa","file":"preprints/Area-controlled-end-replacement-and-the-Bondi-Penrose-inequality-in-the-CKS-class-September-27-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex","line":128,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"079cb80f639fa1e00cd4c0abca0226f5471e1fb8f1b496bbbaabc18c74d25ce9","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Area-controlled-end-replacement-and-the-Bondi-Penrose-inequality-in-the-CKS-class-September-27-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:1dd389f96e686b661882cb33fca7c288edc0c3ccfcd57ea7f23e2d0b70d010fa","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Area-controlled-end-replacement-and-the-Bondi-Penrose-inequality-in-the-CKS-class-September-27-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex#L128"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{prop:replacement}\nLet $(\\Omega,g,K)$ be a smooth connected orientable three-dimensional\nexterior, complete including its nonempty compact smooth boundary,\nwith exactly one end of class \\eqref{eq:cks}. Suppose DEC holds and\n$E_B>|P_B|$. There is a balanced chart such that, for every sufficiently\nlarge $R$, smooth data $(G_R,k_R)$ on the same exterior have the following\nproperties:\n\\begin{enumerate}\n\\item They agree with $(g,K)$ on the compact side of $r=R$ and satisfy DEC.\n\\item For numbers $0\\leq\\varepsilon_R<1$ with $\\varepsilon_R\\to0$,\n      $G_R\\geq(1-\\varepsilon_R)g$ everywhere on $\\Omega$.\n\\item The end is asymptotically flat, with $G_R-\\delta=O_j(r^{-1})$\n      for every fixed finite $j$, and $k_R=0$ sufficiently far out.\n      The constraints are integrable and its charges satisfy\n      $P_R=0$, $E_R=m_B+\\eta_R$, where $0\\leq\\eta_R\\leq2R^{-1/2}$.\n\\end{enumerate}\nThe new exterior is complete and\n$A_{\\min,G_R}(S)\\geq(1-\\varepsilon_R)A_{\\min,g}(S)$.\nNo condition on the boundary expansion is needed."}
